    "roles": ["session", "touring", "band_member"],
    "summary": "Frank Zappa's drummer from 1978 to 1981 (Joe's Garage), then Joni Mitchell's, Sting's from 1990 and one of the most recorded session drummers there is. Taught at Berklee by Gary Chaffee. On Sting's Ten Summoner's Tales he plays odd meters so they feel even: a quarter-note cycle on the hat or ride carried over bars of 5/8 and 7/8, so it comes round every two bars, the kick and snare keeping the bar."
